  <section class="sec" id="mechanism" style="padding-top:48px">
    <div class="tabbox">
      <div class="tabs"><span class="on">Remittance file in, flagged claims out</span></div>
      <div class="body">
        <p>Your payers send remittance files. Tidemark reads each paid line and compares it to the fee in your contract. Any line paid below that fee comes out as a flagged claim, with the amount it was short.</p>
        <p><span class="need">[NEED: how the files and your fee schedule reach Tidemark, and what you get back, in what form, how often]</span></p>
        <div class="diagram" role="img" aria-label="Remittance file goes into Tidemark, flagged claims come out">
          <div class="box dbl"><b>Remittance file</b>The paid lines your payers sent.</div>
          <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="box fill"><b>Tidemark</b>Compares each paid line to your contracted fee.</div>
          <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="box dbl"><b>Flagged claims</b>The lines paid below the fee, and by how much.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

